Hello

I submit that there are serious concerns about the actions of Southwark
Council and possible breaches of its legal duties under the Representation
of the People Acts (various) and related regulations; the Local Democracy,
Economic Development and Construction Act 2009; Localism Act 2011; Data
Protection Act 2018 and related data-protection regulations; as well as the
Human Rights Act 1998. These concerns relate to the way the Council has
handled statutory and democratic processes, its decision-making and
procedures, and the handling and/or disclosure of personal information. I
ask the Court to consider the allegations and the evidence provided, and to
determine whether the Council and/or its officers failed to comply with
their legal duties or acted unlawfully. I have attached supporting evidence
to this email, including relevant documents and correspondence, which I ask
the Court to consider alongside this submission.

--0000000000002be9ff065a52ce92
